% CJK glyph-rendering proof fixture (Group D closure): a real Japanese
% sentence mixing kanji (HanIdeographic script) and hiragana/katakana
% (Kana script), set through stdja-mini's plain `document`/`+p`. No
% `set-font` call anywhere in this file: `document` calls
% `get-initial-context`, which overlays the configured
% `default-font.satysfi-hash` `scripts` block onto `Context::font_scheme`
% automatically (primitives.rs's `prim_get_initial_context`) — so when the
% font root's `scripts` block points `han-ideographic`/`kana` at `ipaexm`
% (exactly what `scripts/download-fonts.sh` writes), this sentence renders
% under the real IPAex face with zero extra wiring here, proving D1a/D1b's
% per-script `font_scheme` end to end through the ordinary document path.

@require: stdja-mini

document (|
  title = {CJK Rendering Proof};
  author = {yasuo};
|) '<
  +p { 日本語のテスト文です }
>
